This product is a modified version of QwFNfer (https://github.com/Apolog1ze-Dev/QwFNfer),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Its baseline (called 2d6837f in the
evidence) is upstream master f955dbf with upstream PRs #10, #12 and #14 merged and two I/O fixes
(bench/qwfn-ref-instrument.patch applies to it). Everything beyond that baseline is this fork's work.

Files modified relative to the baseline (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
  CMakeLists.txt and every file in src/ and tools/ taken from the baseline, except
  src/qwfn_hparams.h and src/qwfn_vocab.h (unchanged); scripts/nvme_ceiling.py is unchanged. Main changes: CPU expert path (routed
  pairs, host reduce, persistent threadpool), readback pack for every verify width, session
  snapshots and shared-prefix checkpoints, pipelined prefill, batched decode-attention
  projections, raw q8_0 K/V gather into flash attention, deterministic expert placement,
  deferred prefetch, per-token NLL/top-k output; and a code-quality refactor of all sources
  (short asserted functions, checked inputs and returns, bounded loops, zero warnings).
New files:
  src/qwfn_check.h, tools/llama_nll.cpp, tools/qwfn_snaptest.cpp, scripts/build.sh,
  scripts/check_rules.py, scripts/check_rules.sh, bench/*, docs/*, patches/*
Removed from upstream: the console, installer/packaging scripts, the Claude Desktop launcher and
  router, the predictor-training and I/O experiment tools, qwfn-run, upstream docs and images.

Third-party components (not modified here unless stated):
  ggml / llama.cpp (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors): used as the kernel
    library, tokenizer and parity reference. One patch is carried in patches/ (ggml-cpu
    mul_mat_id work stealing for 1-2 column batches); it is distributed under the MIT License.
  cpp-httplib and nlohmann/json (MIT) are compiled from llama.cpp's vendor/ tree by the server.

Model weights are not part of this repository and are subject to their own licenses.
